{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/840145-the-faceless-angels","id":840145,"title":"The Faceless Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T13:29:34-08:00","id":840145,"title":"The Faceless Angels","content":"So I was reading a bit online about the pseudo-Anglican hunter Conspiracy, the Knights of St. George and the Faceless Angels they &quot;serve&quot; in a way. Are the Faceless Angels from MtAw's Abyss or they found in Deep Umbra amidst the Starry Void of outer space? I designed an Anomaly called Endrei, Daughter of Faceless Angels and I need to know what she is made of. Well to be precise, what half of her is made of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:26:04-08:00","id":840173,"title":"","content":"There is no canon explanation for what the Angels are. Personally, I use them as Abyssal entities (or, more exactly, the Annunaki themselves- or at leats some of them), but I have made variant versions of them as Astral beings, God Machine angels and Infernal Demons among others. I prefer the Abyssal version out of pure symmetry (just as the Les Mysteres serve spirits, the Faithful of Shulpae are connected to the Devourer, Knights of St Adrian serve the Machine and, in my table, the Cainte Heresy draws its power from the strix).<br /> <br /> Also, Deep Umbra is, I believe, a term from CWoD, especially Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:29:17-08:00","id":840177,"title":"","content":"CofD doesn't have the Deep Umbra; that's Apocalypse/Ascension territory. There's deeper reaches of the Shadow Realm, but I don't believe they're specifically associated with space. Space is, for the most part, just space.<br /> <br /> Witch Finders never comes out and directly asserts that the faceless angels are Abyssal manifestations, and properly speaking, there's not any evidence that the text of the Third Revelation is historically true; there may be no faceless angels, or they may have been a literalization of an apocalyptic vision of something else. If the text is literally true, they're <i>probably</i> not Abyssal manifestations, in that they are something very concrete and defined, if still weird and terrifying. Abyssal manifestations tend to be more abstract. This isn't a 100% solid guideline, so even the great world statues might have been manifestations regardless. Either way, I would suggest that giant statues, even moving statues, are unlikely to have children in the conventional sense, so there's probably more to Endrei's making than just the blood of angels.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, there's definitely a connection between the <i>Goetic Gospels</i> and the Abyss. Knights who study the Gospel of Amon and learn to evoke the Demon King of Nothing have probably been taught some means of aggravating and expanding the natural Abyssal sympathy of the human soul. Probably not <i>all</i> of the Goetic Gospel teachings evoke the Abyss, but it's very much a possibility with the ones that dispel and suppress witchcraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:44:55-08:00","id":840212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/840145-the-faceless-angels?p=840177#post840177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CofD doesn't have the Deep Umbra; that's Apocalypse/Ascension territory. There's deeper reaches of the Shadow Realm, but I don't believe they're specifically associated with space. Space is, for the most part, just space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. However, several books have indicated that space (or at least Earth's solar system) is filled with the God-Machine's Angels, who preserve the earth from astronomical disaster by diverting asteroids and comets. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:08:09-08:00","id":840230,"title":"","content":"Oh, space has weird shit <i>in</i> it, like everywhere else in the CofD. I think Mummy has horrors from beyond the stars, and the idigam were banished to the moon for ages. Just making the distinction that it's not, like, a place that blurs into another dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:55:19-08:00","id":840367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/840145-the-faceless-angels?p=840230#post840230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, space has weird shit <i>in</i> it, like everywhere else in the CofD. I think Mummy has horrors from beyond the stars, and the idigam were banished to the moon for ages. Just making the distinction that it's not, like, a place that blurs into another dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space is nowhere nearly the sole domain of the God-Machine. Luna keeps the fucked-up spirits of space from ruining Earth, and the one that got past her (a spirit of a dying star that got moxed up with an Idigam) was very strange and nasty indeed and Mummy talks at length about the power of the stars and how there are such wonders as black angels that orbit dead stars and consume life force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:39:32-08:00","id":840763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/840145-the-faceless-angels?p=840177#post840177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CofD doesn't have the Deep Umbra; that's Apocalypse/Ascension territory. There's deeper reaches of the Shadow Realm, but I don't believe they're specifically associated with space. Space is, for the most part, just space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops.<br /> <br /> So Mummy is a good place to start on lore wise maybe. Enuff about fluff, could anyone direct me to a book I could use build stats and abilities, please?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:39:07-08:00","id":840890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/840145-the-faceless-angels?p=840173#post840173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no canon explanation for what the Angels are. Personally, I use them as Abyssal entities (or, more exactly, the Annunaki themselves- or at leats some of them), but I have made variant versions of them as Astral beings, God Machine angels and Infernal Demons among others. I prefer the Abyssal version out of pure symmetry (just as the Les Mysteres serve spirits, the Faithful of Shulpae are connected to the Devourer, Knights of St Adrian serve the Machine and, in my table, the Cainte Heresy draws its power from the strix).<br /> <br /> Also, Deep Umbra is, I believe, a term from CWoD, especially Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do like the symmetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}